abl7|n|A bladderlike vessel; a membranous cavity; a cyst; a cell. ; A small bladderlike body in the substance of vegetable, or upon the surface of a leaf. ; A small, and more or less circular, elevation of the cuticle, containing a clear watery fluid. ; A cavity or sac, especially one filled with fluid; as, the umbilical vesicle. ; A small convex hollow prominence on the surface of a shell or a coral. ; A small cavity, nearly spherical in form, and usually of the size of a pea or smaller, such as are common in some volcanic rocks. They are produced by the liberation of watery vapor in the molten mass.	a:8er6,145,1;8gi9,131,8;9bzy,123,19;8xec,75,3~9bzy,123,19;8gi9,131,8;8xec,75,3;8er6,145,1	V:1530,132,3;3j5y,107,5;3j6g,98,9;9tie,75,4;95r1,57,2;1t6n,51,4;1t6x,44,6~3j6g,98,9;1t6x,44,6;3j5y,107,5;9tie,75,4;1t6n,51,4;1530,132,3;95r1,57,2	n:8gi9,126,6~8gi9,126,6	N:5pmv,131,5;1530,116,1;4lub,110,6;5pmt,102,4;3f2c,95,7;95r1,70,5;7vpv,68,14;79in,58,3;8qdh,36,6~7vpv,68,14;3f2c,95,7;4lub,110,6;8qdh,36,6;95r1,70,5;5pmv,131,5;5pmt,102,4;79in,58,3;1530,116,1
